        <mxCell id="zwVLvU2gcYmJ1tXzipiD-156" value="The overall impact of this might also reframe the main issue of alignment.&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Sure there&#39;s the &quot;Any hard optimizer means death&quot;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;But there&#39;s also &lt;b&gt;&quot;Humanity&#39;s final invention will become our only tool -- independently from CAN we use it (takeover) there&#39;s the question of WILL we use it (disempowerment)&quot;.&lt;/b&gt; Then there&#39;s formalizing value lock-in and other things. To prevent this, we have to focus on initial alignment efforts and corrigibility as a primary goal.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Big Yud&#39;s Bankless podcast discussion on how it&#39;s like building a rocket ship but we don&#39;t get to make prototypes and it has to work forever or something.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This reframe could be a far larger umbrella for people to unite under, still attending to the critical issues with takeover. Convince even the tech bros and people interested in winning &quot;the race&quot; who still see AI as a tool that could lead us to massive boons as a danger to the same society that uses it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
